From the keynote table (9. Acid–Base Balance, pH and ABG Interpretation › 9.5 The four primary disorders):
• Disorder: Respiratory acidosis
• pH: ↓
• Primary change: PaCO₂ ↑
• Compensation: Kidneys ↑ HCO₃⁻
• Common causes: Hypoventilation: COPD, opioid/sedative overdose, head injury, exhausted asthma, Guillain–Barré, myasthenia, chest trauma, obesity, ventilator rate too low
• Signs: Drowsiness, headache, confusion, flushed warm skin, tachycardia, CO₂ narcosis, coma$s$, $s$9. Acid–Base Balance, pH and ABG Interpretation › 9.5 The four primary disorders$s$),
