From the keynote table (9. Acid–Base Balance, pH and ABG Interpretation › 9.5 The four primary disorders):
• Disorder: Respiratory alkalosis
• pH: ↑
• Primary change: PaCO₂ ↓
• Compensation: Kidneys ↓ HCO₃⁻
• Common causes: Hyperventilation: anxiety, pain, fever, hypoxia, PE, early sepsis, early salicylate poisoning, pregnancy, high altitude, liver failure, ventilator rate too high
• Signs: Light-headed, tingling/numbness around the mouth and fingers, carpopedal spasm (↓ionised calcium), palpitations$s$, $s$9. Acid–Base Balance, pH and ABG Interpretation › 9.5 The four primary disorders$s$),
