From the keynote table (9. Acid–Base Balance, pH and ABG Interpretation › 9.5 The four primary disorders):
• Disorder: Metabolic acidosis
• pH: ↓
• Primary change: HCO₃⁻ ↓
• Compensation: Lungs ↓ PaCO₂ (Kussmaul breathing)
• Common causes: DKA, lactic acidosis (shock, sepsis, cardiac arrest, seizures), renal failure, diarrhoea, poisoning (methanol, ethylene glycol, salicylates, iron), starvation
• Signs: Deep rapid breathing, headache, confusion, hypotension, arrhythmias, hyperkalaemia$s$, $s$9. Acid–Base Balance, pH and ABG Interpretation › 9.5 The four primary disorders$s$),
