From the keynote table (9. Acid–Base Balance, pH and ABG Interpretation › 9.5 The four primary disorders):
• Disorder: Metabolic alkalosis
• pH: ↑
• Primary change: HCO₃⁻ ↑
• Compensation: Lungs ↑ PaCO₂ (slow shallow breathing)
• Common causes: Vomiting, NG suction, diuretics, hypokalaemia, excess antacids/bicarbonate, massive transfusion (citrate), Cushing's/Conn's
