($s$keynote_cards$s$, $s$17. Anaesthesia and Perioperative Care$s$, false, 919, $s$Local anaesthetic systemic toxicity (LAST)$s$, null, null, $s$perioral numbness, tinnitus, metallic taste, confusion → seizures → arrhythmias/cardiac arrest. Stop injecting, call for help, airway/oxygen, benzodiazepine for seizures, 20% lipid emulsion (1.5 mL/kg bolus then infusion), prolonged CPR. Maximum doses: lidocaine 3 mg/kg (7 mg/kg with adrenaline); bupivacaine 2 mg/kg (most cardiotoxic). Never use adrenaline-containing local anaesthetic on fingers, toes, penis, ears, nose (end arteries — traditional teaching).$s$, null, $s$17. Anaesthesia and Perioperative Care › 17.2 Types of anaesthesia$s$),
