($s$keynote_cards$s$, $s$17. Anaesthesia and Perioperative Care$s$, false, 921, $s$Malignant hyperthermia$s$, null, null, $s$inherited (autosomal dominant); triggered by volatile anaesthetics and suxamethonium. Early signs: rising EtCO₂ (earliest), tachycardia, masseter/jaw rigidity, generalised rigidity, then hyperthermia (late), metabolic and respiratory acidosis, hyperkalaemia, myoglobinuria, arrhythmias. Treatment: stop triggers, hyperventilate with 100% oxygen, dantrolene 2.5 mg/kg IV (repeat to 10 mg/kg; each vial mixed with 60 mL sterile water — needs several staff), active cooling, treat hyperkalaemia and arrhythmias, urine output ≥ 2 mL/kg/hr, ICU. Family testing.$s$, null, $s$17. Anaesthesia and Perioperative Care › 17.3 Anaesthetic emergencies$s$),
